# Line endings
#
# The repository stores LF, and the working tree keeps LF, regardless of the
# machine's `core.autocrlf`. Without this, a Windows clone with autocrlf=true
# checks out CRLF -- which shows up as whole-file diffs, and in a systemd unit
# or shell script a stray CR is a class of bug that costs an afternoon to find.
#
# This project deploys to Linux (nginx + systemd); see deploy/.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary. `text=auto` would otherwise try to normalise these, and a
# "text" blob with CRLF rewritten inside it is a corrupted image.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary

# Keep patch files and SQLite databases untouched.
*.patch binary
*.db    binary
